# ledger/build-cli — what the compiler costs, measured by `wisp cost`
# accepted: the components laws (ui-lead .195): three reads_view laws asked of every item (component_never_called, expand_answers_code, template_reads_once), each one read_whole and one hashed answer per item, moving boxes, retains, releases and reclaims; component_never_called reads each written item's words (item_under retains, an empty word list for an item that can name no component); the bound law asks a component's fns (item_signed_bodies' component arm, component_stmt_at and impl_component_at empty lists; fn_typed and bound_as copies); the two template laws' comprehensions answer an empty list for an item with no template (expands_uncoded, templates_reading_twice)

